 "_note": "THE DATE-RANGE VALIDITY FOLD (U08 · <datepicker> min/max/range/disabledDates/on:month). Dates are ISO civil dates 'YYYY-MM-DD' and ALL arithmetic is the proleptic-Gregorian day count (days_from_civil / civil_from_days) — there is no timezone anywhere in this fold, which is exactly why a DST transition day is one day long here on all three runtimes (the classic 23-hour bug cannot be expressed). SELECTABILITY: within [min, max] when either is set, not in disabledDates, and a real civil date (2026-02-30 is rejected, never coerced). RANGE LAW: with no open start, or with a closed range, a select OPENS a new range {start, end:null}; with an open start a select at or after it CLOSES the range; a select BEFORE it RESTARTS at the new date (never a silent swap — that is the interaction every calendar gets wrong). A close whose span contains a disabled date is refused WHOLE with reason 'range-contains-disabled', because a hotel cannot sell across a blackout night. MONTH LAW: on:month fires only when the visible month actually changes. formsMonthGrid(year, month, firstWeekday) is the grid geometry (firstWeekday is ISO 1=Mon..7=Sun). Expected values come from an independent scratch implementation.",
